  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Local and National-level Dialogue in Lebanon - Phase II: supporting reform options, vision-building and concrete action for service delivery and social cohesion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;overall objective&lt;/strong&gt; of the project is to contribute to &lt;strong&gt;foster a broader societal dialogue to strengthen national consensus and reconciliation.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specifically, it aims to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;1. improve the ability of different actors across the Lebanese political spectrum to engage in the crucial difficult discussions to bring about reconciliation including its political, social, and economic elements, enabling formulation of a shared future vision;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;2. advance and increase abilities of local actors to address historical grievances, sharing of historical narratives to deal with the past, and preconceived images towards the &#xbf;other&#xbf;;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;3. strengthen cohesion among Lebanese actors across the country and increased willingness of these actors to focus on common interests and collectively address challenges in local governance. It will also contribute to enhance social cohesion in its horizontal dimension (interpersonal and intergroup relations) to contribute mitigating the risk of intra-communal tensions that may surge as a result of the recent mass displacement caused by Israel-Hammas conflict.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
